Legacy Loan Calculator (Refactored 2009)

📌 Project Overview

This project is a refactored and modernized version of a legacy C++ Loan/EMI Calculator. The original codebase suffered from "spaghetti code" (all logic in one file), potential integer overflows, lack of validation, and hardcoded values.

This version introduces:

Modular Architecture: Split into header (.h), source (.cpp), and driver (main.cpp) files.

Robust Math: Upgraded to long double to handle large loan amounts without overflow.

Input Validation: strict checks to prevent negative interest rates or loan amounts.

Configurability: Reads default values from config.txt to avoid recompilation for simple changes.

Quality Assurance: Includes GoogleTest unit tests and Doxygen documentation.

📂 Project Structure

legacy-calc-2009/
├── src/                # Source code (Loan.cpp, Loan.h, main.cpp)
├── test/               # Unit tests (test_emi.cpp)
├── lib/                # External libraries (GoogleTest)
├── docs/               # Documentation (Doxygen output)
├── config.txt          # Configuration file for default values
├── Doxyfile            # Doxygen configuration
└── README.md           # This file


 Build & Run Instructions

Prerequisites

G++ Compiler (Supporting C++11 standard)

Git

1. Building the Calculator

Navigate to the project root and run the compiler:

g++ -std=c++11 src/main.cpp src/Loan.cpp -o calc


2. Running the Application

You can run the calculator in two modes:

Mode A: Command Line Arguments
Override defaults by passing flags directly.

-a: Amount (Principal)

-i: Interest Rate (Annual %)

-n: Number of Months

./calc -a 100000 -i 5.5 -n 360


Mode B: Configuration Mode
Run without arguments to load values from config.txt:

./calc


(Edit config.txt to change default values).

🧪 Unit Testing (GoogleTest)

This project uses GoogleTest to verify logic stability. The library is included locally in the lib/ folder to ensure portability.

Compile Tests

Use the following command to link the local GoogleTest library (v1.12.1) with the source code:

g++ -std=c++11 \
    -isystem lib/googletest/googletest/include \
    -isystem lib/googletest/googlemock/include \
    -I lib/googletest/googletest \
    -pthread \
    src/Loan.cpp \
    test/test_emi.cpp \
    lib/googletest/googletest/src/gtest-all.cc \
    -o runTests


Run Tests

Execute the test runner to validate all scenarios (Standard EMI, Negative Input Handling, Large Tenure):

./runTests


Expected Output:

